  "title": "Return is not print",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## The stage hears `say`, not `console.log`\n\n`status()` should **return** `\"locked\"`. Then `Player.say(status())` shows that word on the fox. Printing to the console is a notebook, not the result the next function can use."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "say-return",
      "promptMd": "If `status` only `console.log`s `\"locked\"` and returns nothing, `Player.say(status())` says…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "locked",
          "md": "`locked`"
        },
        {
          "id": "undef",
          "md": "`undefined` — log is not a return",
          "misconceptionId": "print-is-return"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "undef"
    },
